Fri Mar  1 07:42:45 1996  steve clawson  <sclawson@fast.cs.utah.edu>

	* Makerules.man: new file.  Some disgusting rules for installing
	man pages.  Mostly stolen from bsd.man.mk.

	* Updated all Makefile.in's to set the MAN variable for the
	manpages that they need to install.

	* Changed manpages from .man extension to .{mansection}. 
	(ie. machid.man -> machid.1)

	* Makerules: Added -fno-unroll-loops to CFLAGS, since we still use
	-O2.  This is because gcc on the x86 dosen't do loop unrolling
	correctly.

	* Makerules.{man,lib}: Include Makerules.man, and have installman
	as part of their install rule.

